      "drop_accuracy_floor_to_80_does_effecti": "ຫຼຸດລະດັບຕໍ່າສຸດຂອງຄວາມຖືກຕ້ອງລົງເປັນ 80%. WPM ທີ່ໃຊ້ໄດ້ຈິງເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນບໍ?",
      "pros_sustain_95_at_70_wpm_investigate_": "ມືອາຊີບຮັກສາ 95%+ ທີ່ 70+ WPM. ສຳຫຼວດເບິ່ງວ່າເສັ້ນທາງຝຶກແບບໃດພາໄປເຖິງຈຸດນັ້ນ.",
      "a_slower_target_with_high_accuracy_may": "ເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ຊ້າກວ່າແຕ່ຄວາມຖືກຕ້ອງສູງ ອາດຜະລິດຂໍ້ຄວາມໄດ້ຫຼາຍກວ່າຕໍ່ຮອບຝຶກ. ລອງທົດສອບເບິ່ງ.",
      "i_understand_the_tradeoff_explain_in_o": "ຂ້ອຍເຂົ້າໃຈການແລກປ່ຽນແລ້ວ — ອະທິບາຍດ້ວຍຄຳເວົ້າຂອງຕົນເອງ",
      "explain_in_your_own_words_how_do_wpm_a": "ອະທິບາຍດ້ວຍຄຳເວົ້າຂອງເຈົ້າ: WPM, ຄວາມຖືກຕ້ອງ ແລະ ແຮງຊຸກ ພົວພັນກັນແນວໃດ? ເສັ້ນຂອບ Pareto ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າແນວໃດຕໍ່ການຝຶກພິມ?",
      "design_note_discrete_5_zone_marker_par": "ໝາຍເຫດການອອກແບບ: ໝຸດບອກໂຊນແຍກ 5 ລະດັບ. ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Pareto ສະແດງພື້ນທີ່ຂອງການແລກປ່ຽນ. ບໍ່ມີເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ \"ຖືກຕ້ອງ\" — ຕັ້ງໃຈອອກແບບໄວ້ແບບນັ້ນ.",
      "bottom-row_description": "Reach down to z x c v b n m",
      "calming_description": "Seven self-regulation passages a student can type — and read aloud — when feelings get big. Includes box-breathing language, the 5-4-3-2-1 grounding technique, the \"feelings are waves\" frame, the \"pause is not giving up\" reframe, and the \"anxiety lies\" CBT script. Designed by school-psych guidance; not a substitute for clinical care, but a typing-rhythm anchor a student can use in the moment.",
      "capitalization_description": "Shift-key practice. Capitals at sentence starts and proper nouns.",
      "common-words_description": "High-frequency words build real reading fluency.",
      "custom_description": "Your teacher or you can enter any text — spelling lists, IEP goals, science vocab. Not scored for mastery.",
      "focus-errors_description": "Auto-generated practice for YOUR top error keys. Updates after every session based on the heatmap.",
      "growth-mindset_description": "Seven passages on effort, struggle, and the small word YET. Built on Carol Dweck's growth-mindset research and current brain-plasticity science. Pairs with Mind & Body Calming (regulate) and Self-Advocacy (speak up) to form a complete SEL arc — regulate, reframe, advocate. K through high school.",
      "home-row_description": "Start here. Fingers rest on a, s, d, f · j, k, l, ;",
      "maine_description": "Seven hand-written passages about Maine — lighthouses, lobstering, Mount Katahdin, the Penobscot River, Wabanaki history, blueberry barrens, Portland fog. One per grade band, K through high school.",
      "non_english_passages_use_matching_keyboard": "This passage uses the selected language's correct accents or writing system. Choose the matching keyboard layout or input method on your device.",
      "number-row_description": "Reach up to 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0. Same finger-color map as letters.",
      "one-hand-left_description": "Practice with just the left hand. Keys: q w e r t · a s d f g · z x c v b · space.",
      "one-hand-right_description": "Practice with just the right hand. Keys: y u i o p · h j k l ; · n m , . / · space.",
      "passage_description": "AI-generated passage for your grade level and interests. Not locked — anyone can use it.",
      "reduce_motion": "⏸ Motion",
      "save_private_resume_draft_and_return": "Save a private resume draft and return to the menu",
      "self-advocacy_description": "Seven sentences a student with a disability might actually need to say to a teacher, peer, or clinician — typing practice and language rehearsal at once. Covers needing help, asking for breaks, audio learning, fidget tools, IEP testing accommodations, sensory recess needs, and medical lighting accommodations. K through high school.",
      "symbols_description": "Shift + numbers for ! @ # $ % & ( ) and other punctuation.",
      "top-row_description": "Reach up to q w e r t y u i o p"
